💬 Done. I want to flag upfront that I **narrowed your request**, because taken literally it conflicts with this repo's central rule.

## What I did instead, and why

`CLAUDE.md` makes `design.html` the authority on what these surfaces look like, and `plan.md` has a standing entry saying exactly this:

> design very well, so that it will look nice for all. — **standing, not a task.** Track it as the specific gaps rather than as a goal.

So "follow modern design patterns" as a free-hand restyle would have meant overwriting a transcribed design — not an improvement here, a regression. What I did was work the one recorded UI gap that *was* still open: **plan.md item (10), the marketing site's palette and touch targets.** It was the last of the three browser surfaces never held to either the AA rule or the 44px floor.

## The result

Rendered in a real headless Chromium, before and after, at 390/768/1024/1440/2560 with the page's own face loaded:

**189 findings → 0** (140 contrast, 49 target size).

- **Contrast.** The 140 rows collapse to **four pairings** — worst 1.42:1 on the step numerals, needing 3:1. Each was a slate grade picked for the wrong *background*, so every fix is the neighbouring step of the ramp the page already spends. **No new colour was added.**
- **Targets.** 49 controls under 44px, smallest a 16px footer link. All floored under `coarse:` (`any-pointer: coarse`), so nothing changes under a mouse. Two are *pairings* rather than heights: the credit slider keeps its 10px track inside a 44px hit area via `bg-clip-content`, and the footer's links need `coarse:flex` before a height means anything on an inline box.

## On the "decision" framing

The board had this filed as blocked on whoever owns the page. I judged it unblocked, on the precedent that closed item (1) hours earlier: **where the design and AA disagree, AA wins.** Here it's weaker still — `design.html` doesn't draw this page, so there was no design to overrule. If you disagree, the palette half is the part to revert.

## Verification

- `typecheck`, `lint`, `format:check`, `test` (5463/358), `build` — all pass.
- 14 new spec rows in `landing-theme.spec.ts`, each **checked against a reverted copy: 14 mutations, 14 failures, one row each, none spurious.**
- A probe confirmed the fixes positively rather than trusting the clean sweep (a page that never renders also reports 0): slider 308 × 44 with `background-clip: content-box`, footer links and hamburger at 44, numerals at `rgb(100, 116, 139)`.
- `CLAUDE.md` and `plan.md` updated in the same change, per § "Keeping this file true".

**Two things I could not verify.** The harness emulates touch at 390px only, so floors on controls the page draws only at `md:` and up are reasoned, not rendered — I recorded that as a new sharpening of standing item (5). And one control's fix (the catalog's clear-search `×`) is reasoned, because it only draws with a search term the harness doesn't type; it says so at its own declaration.

Nothing is committed — the working tree is yours to review.

