## What I found, and why the scope is what it is

"Follow modern design patterns" ran into this repo's governing rule immediately: `design.html` is a **read-only reference design**, the retailer screens *are* that design, and the operator desk is a transcription of it. Restyling those surfaces isn't a code decision here. The repo has also already done most of what "modern" usually means — AA contrast on all three palettes, 44px touch targets everywhere, focus-managed modals, skeletons, toasts, `inputmode`/`autocomplete` throughout. That work landed in the last few commits.

So I looked for patterns the design *doesn't* govern, and found a real one.

**`apps/landing` respected no motion preference at all.** No `prefers-reduced-motion` block, `scroll-behavior: smooth` on `html`, nine elements animating in, six hover transforms, two smooth `scrollIntoView` calls. The two browser clients have had this rule all along from `global.css` — landing imports nothing, so it stopped at a package border. It stopped at the surface that needed it *most*: the clients declare a transition in fourteen stylesheets between them; this page smooth-scrolls the whole document on every navbar anchor.

Two things made it more than a copy-paste:

- **The stylesheet fix alone is a trap.** `scroll-behavior` is only the default an *unargumented* scroll uses, so an explicit `behavior: 'smooth'` beats the media query — `!important` included. Copying the block and stopping gives a page that reads as fixed, passes every assertion, and still flings the visitor who asked it not to. That half is `src/lib/scroll.ts`.
- **Two dead animations were infinite.** `pulse-subtle` was just unused; `marquee` belonged to the brand strip deleted for claiming twelve partnerships that don't exist — a named animation is the affordance that invites it back. Deleted, with `.animate-shimmer`.

## Verification

- 5 deliberate mutations, each caught by the right rows and no others.
- Built-bundle check: the block is emitted with all four declarations; `marquee`/`shimmer`/`pulseSubtle` appear **zero** times; the two live keyframes appear once each.
- Full suite green (5472 tests / 359 suites), typecheck, lint, format, build.
- Installed the render harness and drew the page: **0 findings**, fonts loaded. That confirms the change moved nothing visible — it does *not* confirm the rule works, since the harness emulates a viewport rather than a reader's settings. I've written that limit down rather than letting the clean sweep imply more than it does.

`CLAUDE.md` and `plan.md` are updated in the same change, as the repo requires.

## Worth knowing

This was invisible to every instrument here — no comment admitted it, and the page has been drawn 21 times without it showing. The check that found it is cheap and generalises: **ask which rule the other surfaces have that this one never imported.** The three surfaces share no stylesheet, so anything in `global.css` is a candidate. I walked that list; the only other entry was `:focus-visible`, and landing is fine there (Tailwind's preflight removes no outline, so the UA ring stands).

If you did want visual modernization — different type scale, spacing rhythm, denser tables, a dark mode — that's genuinely available, but it's a change to `design.html`'s authority rather than to the code, and this repo is emphatic that it's not a decision to make from inside. Tell me which surface and I'll scope it as a design proposal instead.

